e; treated as safe for the party holding the seat.", "Incumbent Becca Balint (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Vermont's at-large district is among the most Democratic-leaning in the country, with a partisan lean of D+17, and first-term incumbent Becca Balint is seeking reelection. University of New Hampshire polls from June through September show her leading Republican Gerald Malloy by 31 to 38 points among likely voters, while a Braun Research survey shows a narrower 15-to-17-point edge. Balint has raised more than $1.1 million and holds a large cash advantage, and prediction markets put her win probability around 97%. The Cook Political Report called the race an easy incumbent win.\n\nMalloy, an Army veteran who won the GOP primary in August, has raised under $200,000 and faces a steep structural disadvantage in a state that has never elected a Republican to this seat in the modern era. The main question is the size of the margin rather than the outcome, with the tighter Braun figures the chief source of uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9976, "margin": 26.51}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9993, "margin": 30.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9992, "margin": 30.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9998, "margin": 33.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9994, "margin": 32.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9993, "margin": 30.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.999, "margin": 26.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 26.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9993, "margin": 26.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 25.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9994, "margin": 26.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.999, "margin": 26.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9977, "margin": 25.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9988, "margin": 25.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9993, "margin": 26.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9974, "margin": 25.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9989, "m